			<div class="content" id="post-content-4856665">
									

<p>Thanks for the feedback and criticism, and I would like to discuss this whole affair further.</p>
<p>The real problem here is that there is just not enough space to tell this story in under 400 words, as an elevator pitch. This is an extremely complex story that consists of multiple SCP stories all weaving into the actual narrative.</p>
<p><strong>*SPOILER ALERT BELOW!</strong>*</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>To be clear: it activates if the crank is turned and not just if you like, ask it via particular audio frequencies? If so, what does 'will respond to' mean?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If audio frequencies are played for it, it will activate remotely.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Not really a fan of this angle. It feels too much like you're just throwing out a bunch of vague ideas you find kinda interesting in an attempt to make the position of the Architect more interesting, but it doesn't really and it doesn't really come across as interesting to me. More to the point, I'm not really sure how the Foundation figure out the Architect exists or like, what that actually means for this SCP or the world at large?</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Generally I'm not a fan of things that just make you go crazy, particularly in a way that causes you to forget a lot; since like…it's super overplayed and often feels…kinda problematic and like it stigmatizes mental illness more. More to the point, it's also an effect that's really hard to convey in an interesting way within the confines of a SCP article.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well&#8230; That's kind of the point really. It's a mystery that will begin to unravel with each new artifact that is found. At the stage of the automaton, the architect is nothing more than what seems to be collaborative delusion or effect of the psychosis caused by the very intentional hiding of his magic through psychological means. Think of them as a sort of trap card to hide his magic from prying eyes, which is actually a method for creating dimensional gates that he has lost. while it seems to be almost a chaotic effect at the surface, further investigations will note that it is not simply randomly causing mental illnesses, but rather the mathematical sequences hidden within its geometry are causing unknown preexisting conditions within subjects to rapidly grow in strength and effect. So someone who originally would have gotten Alzheimer's in their late 70's or 80's rapidly advances to first stage Alzheimer's within a few days. When the defense can't find a logical disease to latch onto, it instead creates a feedback effect upon a particular psychological mindset and amplifies it to extremes, like Pyromania or Schizophrenia. It is less creating effects at random and more amplifying what is already there in the mind in an active attempt to hide secrets. This can be made aware through research and the existence of the architect will be made aware of through interviews of isolated test subject interviews. the most important of which being that while researching and experimenting on the SCP and its products, two things are noted. One, that the images it produces are actually small pieces of larger puzzles that are meant to create literal dimensional gateways, and two, that the mathematically created &quot;psychological traps&quot; seem to have no effect on subjects who suffer from high functioning autism, which gives them the ability to compartmentalize the traps and seemingly avoid them as they put together the pieces of this massive puzzle.</p>
<p>While there is a story intended here, most of it will be displayed through experiment procedures and interviews, but do keep in mind that cosmic horror is a specific type of horror, and not all the answers can or will be explained fully. I feel bad even explaining this outright to you as it's more meant to be pieced together through the story of the artifacts and interviews. The lack of cohesion is very intentional because it is a mystery that will be slowly put together as the story unfolds. Though it's effects and its physical being seem to be completely disconnected from one another, they are very much connected to one another. It will just take a certain type of person to be the key to unlock the mystery.</p>
<p>And the story I have in mind certainly cannot be told in under 400 words on a pitch. This is by no means something that could be elevator pitched, to say the least, and yes it will be incredibly difficult to achieve. But that's partially the reason I am doing it.</p>
</div>
